{
  "id": "elasar",
  "name": "Eleazar",
  "title": "Aaron's son and Israel's high priest",
  "era": "exodus",
  "lifespan": "c. 1500–1400 BC",
  "summary": "Eleazar was the third son of Aaron and succeeded him as high priest in Israel after Aaron's death. He served faithfully under Moses' leadership and played a key role in distributing the land of Canaan under Joshua. He became the ancestor of the priestly line that served at the tabernacle and later in the temple.",
